# The contract this portal is generated against.
#
# The OPERATOR contract, not the traveller one. Different document, different
# base path, different auth, and a tenant boundary the traveller API does not
# have: `operator_id` is read from the session row and is never accepted as a
# parameter in any position.
#
# The intent is that both frontends pin one yuvoy-api commit, so they cannot be
# reasoning about different versions of the same backend. They agree today:
# `yuvoy-app` is on this same ref. The two documents are separate files, so a
# change to one says nothing about the other — this bump touches only the
# operator document, and yuvoy-app's bump to the same ref touched only the
# traveller one.
#
# `pnpm contract:check` fails the build if this copy stops matching the ref.
repo=yuvoy-in/yuvoy-api
path=contracts/operator-openapi.yaml
# 7 Sep 2026, sixth bump. Forward from 87175540e3ec, pinned this morning.
# Diffed as a parsed schema tree, not as text — the defects that made that
# necessary are on yuvoy-api#92 and #103. PURELY ADDITIVE and narrow: ONE
# endpoint changed, one field added, three descriptions written. Nothing
# removed, no `required:` list grown, no requestBody made required.
#
# Consumed in this change (yuvoy-api#119):
#   - `GET /media` now returns `kind`, `video` or `image`, spelled as the
#     traveller document spells it so nothing has to translate. This closes the
#     gap the previous pin recorded: the operator's own library held both and
#     had nothing on the wire to tell them apart.
#
# **`kind` is never inferred from `durationSeconds`**, and the contract now
# says so itself. A clip that is still `uploaded` or `processing` has no
# duration either, so the first thing an operator sees after posting a reel
# would be that reel labelled a photograph. Guessing wrong there is worse than
# not guessing, which is why the previous build labelled nothing at all.
#
# Learned from the same change, and it is the reason the tile was rebuilt:
#   - `posterUrl` is ABSENT ON MOST CLIPS — a poster is only stored once the
#     provider has produced one, and an unpublished clip has no public URL.
#     270 of 342 clips had none when this was written. A row with no poster
#     still has a `kind` and a `state` and has to render as something, so the
#     tile no longer assumes a picture exists.
#   - For a photograph the picture IS the poster, and it is now built at read
#     time from configuration, at every state rather than only when published.
#     Fixed API-side in the same PR: the operator's own photographs previously
#     came back with no `posterUrl` at all.
#
# The remaining half — a signed poster for an unreviewed clip — is deliberately
# NOT in this change and is tracked as yuvoy-api#121. An unreviewed clip with a
# public poster URL is what the signed-URL design exists to prevent.
#
# Known gap, verified rather than assumed: `not_selling` on
# `OperatorExperience.status` and the 409 `operator_not_sellable` on
# `POST /requests/{id}/accept` (yuvoy-operator#28) are NOT in this document.
# The issue describes them as shipped in migration 0053; master carries
# migrations to 0051 only and no branch has more. The string-keyed halves of
# that issue are built anyway and are inert until the values arrive; the typed
# half waits for the merge.
